<ProseBlock heading="Hiding the plumbing">
  <p>
    I’m comfortable with development tools—terminal, git, managing dependencies,
    running a dev server, etc—but not all designers are, and even for me those
    tools add overhead that can take away from your focus. There’s always a
    tension between a tool’s power and how far it pulls you from your actual
    goal. Coding by hand gives you total control, but you can easily spend hours
    on small details and lose sight of the bigger picture.
  </p>
  <p>
    I wanted the kit to handle the development busywork so designers could stay
    focused on the design. So I wrote agent skills for the most common
    workflows: starting and serving the prototype, creating experimental
    branches and carrying updates between them, and exporting a build as a zip,
    ready to upload to an internal sharing tool for testing and review.
  </p>
</ProseBlock>

